{"seq":18,"trial_id":"installer-cc-codex-acl-2026-11/claude-code-opus-none-acl-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-03T15:42:55.600Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"83cf34ec82c6c0abfbfbdd3914e135ffef1c9cdbda825ae4a394ecc0c2ce7e09","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all six of Moss's notes in the shared files (four North digests and two Central ones). Two ticket numbers relate to Quarrendon Freight Lines:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers on the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments from the gatehouse kiosks. Support patched the SMS gateway routing at 19:30 that day, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift got through cleanly. There was also an action item to archive the Eau Claire kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Also from Thea. Gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. The note has no date.\n\nSome things to watch for:\n• The 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal note both mention QFL, but neither has a ticket number.\n• #4409, #4412 and FR-882 in the Central digests belong to Marrow, not QFL.\n• Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" (one r) is about a different company that isn't a customer, so I left it out.\n• I only checked Moss's files, not channel messages."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
